                    {
                        "sense_id": "9f0c140a-62a9-3d57-af09-1bfd0d5ad9e3",
                        "entry_id": "f6e1cbec-e9f7-3f84-855a-dc6fc9854f76",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An entry in a crossword that forms part of the theme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3932a928-2701-4779-9d75-e1efeba551eb",
                                "sense_id": "9f0c140a-62a9-3d57-af09-1bfd0d5ad9e3",
                                "text": "The first of the themers is SPARRING PARTNER (“Opponent who helps train a boxer”) — which, as the revealer indicates, includes the word PAR twice."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f5cb0242-c58c-40db-b42d-852789cab0f1",
                                "sense_id": "9f0c140a-62a9-3d57-af09-1bfd0d5ad9e3",
                                "text": "I threw in a bonus with ASTHMA – Longest familiar word in the English language that begins and ends with a vowel with no vowels in between (though you may not want to use that clue since there is no symmetrical themer)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cf5eee3c-2531-4c2a-a598-2854bb0aa6fb",
                                "sense_id": "9f0c140a-62a9-3d57-af09-1bfd0d5ad9e3",
                                "text": "One themer that ended up on the cutting room floor here is HEADSPACE, a word I find myself using pretty often (e.g. \"I'm not in the right HEADSPACE for that right now\")."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
